# Conversion strategies

Every strategy is only a per-year dollar list. The engine still draws from
tax-deferred accounts, taxes the conversion, and deposits Roth. Strategies
do not change income, expenses, withdrawals, or RMD rules.

## Strategies

| Value | What it schedules |
| ---- | ---- |
| `even` | Convertible total (or `convertAmount`) spread across the pre-RMD window. |
| `immediate` | Same target in year 1. Engine caps at that year's live pre-RMD balance. |
| `fillBracket` | Each year, room to the top of `targetBracketRate` (12% / 22% / 24%; default 22%) from one no-conversion projection. |
| `irmaa` | Each year, room just under the next IRMAA MAGI floor above baseline MAGI. Top tier: no MAGI cap. |
| `depleteByRmd` | Walk balances (grow, withdraw, convert `remaining / yearsLeft`, then deposits) so tax-deferred empties by RMD. |
| `minTax` | Lowest lifetime income tax: federal + state paid over the plan, the same `taxesTotal` the results show as Lifetime taxes. Tax on tax-deferred money left at the end is not counted. Starts from the best of no conversion and every other strategy, then nudges each conversion year up or down (step halves to $500) keeping changes that lower that total. Ignores Medicare and inheritance size. |
| `manual` | User-edited `manualSchedule`. Default for new plans. Shown first as Manual. Editing a year in the Conversion wizard (or on even/immediate) switches here. |

`buildConversionSchedule(household, refs)` is the switch. Fill-bracket and
IRMAA need live federal / Medicare tables via `refs`.

## Monthly shortfall limit

`optimizer.maxMonthlyShortfall` (missing = off) caps every strategy, Manual
included. `buildConversionSchedule` runs the strategy, then
`capConversionsToShortfall` (`src/lib/optimizer/shortfall.ts`) walks the years
in order and bisects each year's amount down until that year's `surplus`
(monthly) is at least `-maxMonthlyShortfall`. A year already short by more than
the limit with no conversion converts nothing. The menu's switch next to the
Conversion strategy heading sets it to `DEFAULT_MAX_MONTHLY_SHORTFALL` ($1,000)
or clears it. Strategy scores and Minimum taxes go through the same cap
(Minimum taxes searches uncapped, then is capped).

## Menu

`ConversionStrategyMenu` sits above the plan Timeline on desktop, and in the
mobile Plan details modal (not in the Conversion wizard step). Manual is first. Each row shows **Total impact**
from `scoreConversionStrategies`: one shared no-conversion baseline, then one
Roth run per option. Formula lives in `totalImpact()` (same as the results
header): inheritance + tax savings + Medicare Part B. After-tax assets at
RMD are excluded (same estate snapshot as inheritance, just earlier).
Choosing Manual with no saved years copies the current live schedule
so the year grid has numbers to edit. Each row has a "?" tooltip
(`STRATEGY_HELP` in `labels.ts`).

Fill-bracket is one row that reads Fill {12% / 22% / 24%} bracket. The dollar
is the selected rate; all three rates are precomputed.

## Persistence

- Missing optimizer or unknown strategy → `manual`.
- `manual` with no schedule stays `manual` (engine spreads convertible evenly).
- Explicit `manualSchedule` stays `manual`.
- Missing `targetBracketRate` on `fillBracket` → `0.22`.

## Gotchas

- `minTax` runs a few hundred projections (up to about 150ms). `minTaxSchedule`
  keeps a one-entry cache keyed on the household minus `optimizer`, so the
  menu and the results share one search. Its schedule ignores every
  `optimizer` field, including `convertAmount`.
- `minTax` targets the results' Lifetime taxes number, so it never shows more
  lifetime tax than no conversion or any other strategy. It does not count the
  tax heirs will owe on a leftover tax-deferred balance, so on a plan with
  steady income and a short RMD window it may convert little or nothing.

- Fill-bracket / IRMAA use baseline income only (one pass). Later-year
  balances may be lower; the engine caps.
- Brackets and IRMAA floors are not inflation-adjusted in the projection.
- `allowOverConvertible` and `convertAmount` apply to even / immediate /
  manual, not to the computed strategies.
- Editing a year in the Conversion wizard copies the live schedule into
  `manual` and does not keep a computed strategy live.
